Current writeAtomic close in try and catch double close. Should have injection seam for open/rename/rm and directory sync. I can export `writeAtomic`? Currently private. For unit tests could test through saveReport with injected options if export new testable `writeAtomic` not ideal. Plan explicitly injected fs seam, so export function maybe public internal API. Could export `writeAtomic` with third optional `AtomicFileSystem` parameter. Tests import it directly, but production helper export is legitimate reusable function. Type `FileHandle` from fs/promises. Should simplify by `writeAtomic(filePath, body, fs=atomicFs)` where fs includes `open`, `rename`, `rm`. Directory sync uses `open(path.dirname(filePath),'r')`, handle.sync close. That uses same injected open. Tests can use actual temp files wrapped around real functions to simulate. But `open` overloaded types complex. Could define narrow custom interface:
```
interface AtomicHandle {
 writeFile(body:string):Promise<void>;
 sync():Promise<void>;
 close():Promise<void>;
}
interface AtomicFs {
 open(filePath:string, flags:string, mode?:number):Promise<AtomicHandle>;
 rename(oldPath,newPath):Promise<void>;
 rm(path,options:{force:true}):Promise<void>;
}
const realAtomicFs: AtomicFs = { open, rename, rm };
```
