```
let handle;
try {
 handle=await open
 await write
 await sync
} catch(error) {
 await rm(tmp,{force:true})
 throw error
} finally {
 if(handle) await handle.close()
}
try {
 await rename
 await syncDirectory(path.dirname(filePath),fs)
} catch(error) {
 await rm(tmp,{force:true})
 throw error
}
```
If close throws, finally rejects, but tmp cleanup? The catch before finally won't catch finally close error. Temp remains. Should have robust exactly once and cleanup on close failure. Better:
```
const handle = await fs.open(tmp,'w',0o600)
try {
  try {
    await handle.writeFile(body)
    await handle.sync()
  } finally {
    await handle.close()
  }
} catch(error) {
  await fs.rm(tmp,{force:true})
