Exactly once close via inner finally, catches close error outer and removes temp. If write fails and close also fails, close error replaces write error. Plan only double-close cannot throw; ideally preserve original error? Could handle:
```
let operationError: unknown
try {...} catch(error){operationError=error}
let closeError
try await close catch...
if operationError or closeError cleanup and throw operationError ?? closeError
```
Overkill. Standard try/finally accepted. But data safety errors should preserve original. Could simple:
```
try {
 await handle.writeFile
 await handle.sync
 await handle.close()
} catch(error) {
 await rm(tmp)
