const directory = await fs.open(path.dirname(filePath),'r')
try { await directory.sync() } finally { await directory.close() }
```
Exactly once close for directory too. If sync dir fails after rename, catch removes tmp (already renamed, rm force no effect) and throws though file replaced. Can't roll back; report digest handles pair. Tests should verify directory sync called. If directory close fails, catch rm no effect. Fine.
